# Hand-placed, not part of the fabric: the two air conditioners on the back wall, the water
# pipe up the +x end wall, the washing line out back, and the four concrete steps at the doors.
# Carried verbatim from the old bunkhouse.part -- the shell's footprint and wall positions did
# not move, so these coordinates still land exactly where they used to.

# air conditioners, +z back wall
piece models/shapes/box.obj     -4.0 2.0 3.06    0.9 0.7 0.5   0 0 0   0.76 0.79 0.95  tex concrete_rough 0.8
piece models/shapes/box.obj      4.0 2.0 3.06    0.9 0.7 0.5   0 0 0   0.76 0.79 0.95  tex concrete_rough 0.8
# water pipe, +x end wall
piece models/shapes/cylinder.obj 8.05 0.4 0      0.10 3.4 0.10  0 0 0  0.76 0.79 0.95  tex concrete_rough 0.8
# washing line, +z side
piece models/shapes/cylinder.obj -3.0 0 4.5      0.08 1.8 0.08  0 0 0  0.83 0.85 0.98  tex concrete_rough 1.0
piece models/shapes/cylinder.obj  3.0 0 4.5      0.08 1.8 0.08  0 0 0  0.83 0.85 0.98  tex concrete_rough 1.0
piece models/shapes/box.obj       0 1.8 4.5      6.0 0.03 0.03  0 0 0  0.85 0.85 0.85
# four concrete steps, one at each door
piece models/shapes/plate.obj   -6.0 0.35 -3.5    1.3 0.8 0.8   0 0 0   1.74 1.71 1.58  tex painted_wall 0.7
piece models/shapes/plate.obj   -2.0 0.35 -3.5    1.3 0.8 0.8   0 0 0   1.74 1.71 1.58  tex painted_wall 0.7
piece models/shapes/plate.obj    2.0 0.35 -3.5    1.3 0.8 0.8   0 0 0   1.74 1.71 1.58  tex painted_wall 0.7
piece models/shapes/plate.obj    6.0 0.35 -3.5    1.3 0.8 0.8   0 0 0   1.74 1.71 1.58  tex painted_wall 0.7
